      "writtenOn": "2022-07-29T21:32:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Score needs to exactly match the present_fields. The policy must always be an exact match.\n\nFor policies that overlap, the policy which is more precise should be used.\n\nEx: Policy 1 with only port; Policy 2 with port/ip. Policy 2 should be used if matching.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 190,
        "startChar": 12,
        "endLine": 190,
        "endChar": 17
      },
      "revId": "8b965f2c1136c8ef5758041e77c2c8b3a05e0deb",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c209ad07_a7b4d4a0",
        "filename": "bpf_progs/dscpPolicy.c",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 190,
      "author": {
        "id": 1003247
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-07-29T21:58:44Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "That\u0027s what this does.  It gives more precise dst port ranges - ie. shorter ones - a bigger score, so they outscore less precise dst port ranges.\n\nAmong other things this makes a \u0027dst port 5\u0027 beat out \u0027dst port 2-7\u0027 which in turn beats \u0027dst port 0-65535\u0027 which is now fully equivalent to no dst port specified.",
      "parentUuid": "0dd6ec44_bfaafe36",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 190,
        "startChar": 12,
        "endLine": 190,
        "endChar": 17
      },
      "revId": "8b965f2c1136c8ef5758041e77c2c8b3a05e0deb",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3f18ab1b_479df03e",
        "filename": "bpf_progs/dscpPolicy.c",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 190,
      "author": {
        "id": 1594463
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-07-29T22:02:47Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think it does exactly that.\nThe new version of the program will check all present fields, and if *any* of them mismatch it will go on to checking the next rule. So this point is only reached if all present fields match.\n\nAfter this change, policies with smaller port ranges will outrank policies with larger port ranges. (But the port range must always be set.)",
      "parentUuid": "0dd6ec44_bfaafe36",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 190,
        "startChar": 12,
        "endLine": 190,
        "endChar": 17
      },
      "revId": "8b965f2c1136c8ef5758041e77c2c8b3a05e0deb",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
